# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pyoneer generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime artifacts
*.log
*.prof
*.lprof
saves/
screenshots/

# AI relay bundles. Every use of the editor's prompt strip writes a
# NNNN-slug/ directory here (editor/core/request.py's write_bundle), carrying
# a snapshot of the vocabulary, the author's notes and the project's absolute
# path. They are one exchange's scratch, not source: a committed one goes
# stale the day the vocabulary moves. write_bundle creates the directory on
# demand and the editor's watcher re-arms after each ship, so nothing needs
# it to exist in git.
editor/requests/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PyCharm
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .idea/ is deliberately NOT ignored wholesale. Pyoneer relies on the
# sourceFolder entries in .idea/Pyoneer.iml to put scripts/core, scripts/game,
# config/, etc. on sys.path -- that is what makes the bare imports
# ("from component import GameComponent", "from event_types import ...")
# resolve. The .iml is build configuration, not editor preference, so it is
# tracked. Only the per-developer machine state is ignored below.
.idea/workspace.xml
.idea/tasks.xml
.idea/usage.statistics.xml
.idea/dictionaries/
.idea/shelf/
.idea/httpRequests/
.idea/dataSources/
.idea/dataSources.local.xml
.idea/**/sonarlint/
.idea/copilot/
.idea/copilot.data.migration.*.xml
*.iws

# Other editors
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dropbox
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The working tree lives inside Dropbox, which drops sync metadata into every
# folder and forks files it cannot merge. Neither belongs in history.
desktop.ini
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr
.dropbox.cache
*conflicted copy*
*Conflicted Copy*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Icon?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: art source & foreign engine files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~17 MB of files under data/graphics/ that the pygame runtime never loads:
# layered art sources (.psd/.pdn/.xcf) and leftover XNA/MonoGame content-
# pipeline artifacts (.xnb/.mgcontent). The exported .png sprites are what the
# engine actually reads. Uncomment to keep them out of the repo -- but move
# them somewhere safe first, since they are the editable originals.
#*.psd
#*.pdn
#*.xcf
#*.sai
#*.xnb
#*.mgcontent

# Agent worktrees (transient; created by the Workflow tool)
.claude/worktrees/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party art
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/graphics/ is NOT tracked and was removed from history. The tileset and
# character sheets present locally match the RPG Maker VX Ace RTP by filename
# and by exact pixel dimensions (TileA2 512x384, Actor1/People1 384x256,
# IconSet 384x3072). That licence covers use inside RPG Maker projects and
# does not permit redistributing the assets, which a public repo would do.
#
# One unqualified line, and it stays that way. A negation here would have to
# spell the exact path a licensed sheet occupies on the author's machine
# (!data/graphics/tilesets/System/TileA2.png), so `git add` would stage HIS
# file. What ships instead is data/art/ -- the generated pack, TRACKED, one
# prefix swap away -- and scripts/core/art.py's resolve_art puts them in
# order: data/graphics/ wins whenever it has the file, data/art/ answers when
# it does not. See docs/ASSETS.md and #TAG:art_two_roots.
#
# data/art/ is deliberately NOT listed below. If a future rule would sweep it
# up, that rule is the thing to narrow.
data/graphics/

# Art cropped in through the tileset import dialog. Third-party images land
# here, so new ones stay out of the repo by default. NOTE this does not untrack
# what is already committed: the sample pushed in ef0ea70 is still versioned and
# public, and only `git rm --cached` takes it back out.
data/maps/tilesets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio you may play but not redistribute
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/sound/ is the author's own audio: the override root
# scripts/core/audio.py looks at FIRST. Same rule as data/graphics/ and for
# the same reason -- a licence to play is not a licence to redistribute, and
# a public repo redistributes. What ships instead is data/audio/, TRACKED,
# one prefix swap away, with its provenance in data/audio/CREDITS.md.
# data/audio/ is deliberately NOT listed here.
data/sound/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NovelAI pipeline state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/nai/ keeps its working state here: the append-only ledger (account
# balances), proof rows, the LOCK and INFLIGHT markers, request/response
# blobs, mannequin renders and generated sprites. None of it is source.
# Generated NovelAI output stays out of the repo until the author decides
# otherwise, having read NovelAI's terms for generated images; promoting a
# sprite to data/art/ is a deliberate, by-hand step, never the tool's.
#
# data/reference/sprites/ is deliberately NOT listed: those are CC0 sheets
# drawn by people, committed with their provenance in its CREDITS.md.
data/nai/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys live in the Windows USER environment, never in a file here: the NovelAI
# key is NAI_KEY, read with os.environ. These patterns exist so a dotenv file
# someone creates anyway cannot be committed. tools/check_secrets.py is the
# second net, for a key pasted into a tracked file under any name.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
